{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1756,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Napoleon's best chance at Waterloo may have been sitting at breakfast, eating strawberries.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 79
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Belgium, June eighteenth, eighteen fifteen. Napoleon, back from exile, has a new army. In front of him, Wellington. Somewhere east, the Prussians, beaten two days earlier.",
   "from": 82,
   "to": 319
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A day earlier, Napoleon sent Marshal Grouchy and over thirty thousand men after the Prussians, to keep them away.",
   "from": 323,
   "to": 456
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It rains all night. Napoleon waits for the mud to dry, giving the Prussians time.",
   "from": 459,
   "to": 559
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Miles away, Grouchy is at breakfast. Strawberries, the story goes. Then a low rumble, from the west. Cannons.",
   "from": 563,
   "to": 740
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "gerard",
   "text": "Marshal, we must march to the guns!",
   "from": 743,
   "to": 793
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "grouchy",
   "text": "My orders are to follow the Prussians.",
   "from": 797,
   "to": 876
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So he keeps chasing, into a rear guard at Wavre. Most Prussians have already slipped away toward Waterloo.",
   "from": 880,
   "to": 996
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "blucher",
   "text": "Forward! Faster!",
   "from": 999,
   "to": 1037
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "By late afternoon, they crash into Napoleon's side.",
   "from": 1041,
   "to": 1109
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "His last attack breaks. His army runs.",
   "from": 1112,
   "to": 1184
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Wellington called it the nearest run thing you ever saw.",
   "from": 1187,
   "to": 1248
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Now, what if Grouchy had turned around? Some historians say he'd have arrived too late anyway.",
   "from": 1252,
   "to": 1367
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Even winning that day probably wouldn't have saved Napoleon. Austrian and Russian armies were already marching on France.",
   "from": 1370,
   "to": 1508
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Most historians think he'd still have lost, just somewhere else.",
   "from": 1512,
   "to": 1585
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the strawberries probably didn't change the war. Just which village gave us \"meet your Waterloo.\"",
   "from": 1589,
   "to": 1732
  }
 ],
